  "question": {
    "text": "If the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pKa</mi></math> of lactic acid is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>, then the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pH</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>005</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> calcium lactate solution at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is __________ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> (Nearest integer)<br />&nbsp;"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "85",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Concentration of calcium lactate =&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>005</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math></p><p>concentration of lactate ion =&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>005</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math></p><p>Calcium lactate is a salt of weak acid + strong base</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp;Salt hydrolysis will take place for a basic salt:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>pH</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>pKa</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>logC</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>log</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>01</mn><mo>)</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mn>85</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p>"
  }
